Z||000002||Black88GT||09-14-2001||01:19 AM||||Highly unlikely.  Only way that would happen would be on a limited basis like Vietnam, or at the worst like WW2, but that would be a global conflict which is looking less and less likely as the days go on.  We have enough active duty/reserves to deal with a few small Arab countries.  <P>Remember, just because your drafted doesn't necessarily mean your going to the front lines.  My grandfather was drafted and worked in a wharehouse for about 5 months but then requested to go fight (he's not the type to be couped up in a wharehouse) and my other grandfather trained soldiers in the USA.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jaygee79||09-14-2001||01:22 AM||||i think (and hope) that if you are the only son then you can be one of the last to go (but maybe only if your mother requests it. i dunno)||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tonker||09-14-2001||01:26 AM||||I doubt it. That might happen if a full blown war erupts, but how likely is that? Who are you going to fight? This isn't the sort of thing that is dealt with by sending in boatload after boatload of marine (or whatever service interests you).<P>More than likely it will consist of the Navy and Airforce sending in some cruise missiles, maybe some bombing. Some limited ground forces might be called into it. My guess would be that this is better handles by a SEAL team, or what we call the JTF here, which is basically a tactical anti-terrorist force.<P>If it's found that a state is involved in some way there might be a multinational coalition attack on them.<P>I guess I could basically have said in a more short-winded fashion: I don't see conscription for anything short of a full-blown war and that isn't very likely in this case.||||reg||1
