Z||000007||maryjane||09-14-2001||04:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tonker:<BR><B>I doubt it. That might happen if a full blown war erupts, but how likely is that? Who are you going to fight? This isn't the sort of thing that is dealt with by sending in boatload after boatload of marine (or whatever service interests you).<P>More than likely it will consist of the Navy and Airforce sending in some cruise missiles, maybe some bombing. Some limited ground forces might be called into it. My guess would be that this is better handles by a SEAL team, or what we call the JTF here, which is basically a tactical anti-terrorist force.<P>If it's found that a state is involved in some way there might be a multinational coalition attack on them.<P>I guess I could basically have said in a more short-winded fashion: I don't see conscription for anything short of a full-blown war and that isn't very likely in this case.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I covered this in another thread, but will repeat it here. If you think what you posted above is the way it's going to be, I feel sorry. Do you think we'd be calling up 50,00<BR>reservists to launch a few cruise missles or send in a seal team or two? Have you seen the terrain in Afganistan? To root out terrorist groups, it's going to take grunts combined with air power, and a lot of them. Wake up man, smell the gunpowder. It ain't going to be Zeus throwing lightning bolts. This is going to take months, maybe a year or longer. Those in combat are going to need replacements and rotating out of the shi* once in a while. The draft? Probably not for the first few weeks, but, I wouldn't count it out if it lasts a long time and we take a lot of casualties. <P>||||reg||1
