Z||000022||Fformula88||09-15-2001||10:58 PM||||Just wanted to fill in everyone with some of the new draft laws... they are different from the Vietnam draft.<P>The big difference is for college students... those who are drafted and in college can only deffer their entrance until the end of the current term they are in.<P>Age... they start with those men who are to turn age 20 in the year of the draft.  Example... the first round in a draft lottery now would be anyone who was born in 1980.  They would then go up the ladder to 25 if needed (and thats would be an awful lot of troops.)<P>As for enlisting to pick your service... this is what my father did when he found out he would be drafted for Vietnam.  He did join the Air Force and ended up stationed in Chayenne, WO working on Nuclear Missle Silo computers!||||reg||1
